---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="About — Cyan Studio" description="About the artist and the cyanotype process." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="about-grid">
				<div class="about-text">
					<p class="page-label">About</p>
					<h1>A little bit about me.</h1>
					<p>
						Hi, I'm Krista. Thanks for visiting my page. I'm based out of Ucluelet, BC on the wet west coast of Vancouver Island.
						I've been grateful to call this place my home for the past eight years, living and working on the traditional territory of the Yuułuʔiłʔatḥ Government.
					</p>
					<p>
						As a biologist by training (and self-professed kelp nerd), it was here — surrounded by rugged coastline, rainforest, and stunning marine diversity — that I discovered the cyanotype process.
						Solar printing felt like the perfect intersection between science and creativity, allowing me to share the beauty of the coast in a way that's a little nerdy, a little whimsical, and a whole lot of blue.
					</p>
					<p>
						Every print is unique and carefully created using archival quality paper and packaging materials, so your piece will last.
					</p>

					<div class="about-divider"></div>

					<h2>The process</h2>
					<div class="process-list">
						<div class="process-item">
							<span class="p-num">01</span>
							<div>
								<strong>Forage</strong>
								<p>Seaweeds and botanicals are collected by hand from the shoreline and forest — ferns, flowers, kelp, sea lettuce, and whatever the tide brings in.</p>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="process-item">
							<span class="p-num">02</span>
							<div>
								<strong>Prep</strong>
								<p>Archival watercolour paper is coated with a light-sensitive cyanotype solution — a mixture of ferric ammonium citrate and potassium ferricyanide — and left to dry in the dark.</p>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="process-item">
							<span class="p-num">03</span>
							<div>
								<strong>Compose &amp; expose</strong>
								<p>Botanicals are arranged on the coated paper before being placed in direct sunlight.</p>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="process-item">
							<span class="p-num">04</span>
							<div>
								<strong>Develop</strong>
								<p>The print is exposed to UV for a select amount of time before being rinsed in water. A blueprint is revealed.</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<aside class="about-aside">
					<div class="aside-card">
						<h3>Originals</h3>
						<p>Each original is one-of-a-kind — no two are ever exactly the same. Signed and titled on the reverse.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="aside-card">
						<h3>Reproductions</h3>
						<p>Select reproductions are available as fine art prints — a more accessible way to bring a piece of the coast into your home.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="aside-card">
						<h3>Materials</h3>
						<p>All prints are made on acid-free, archival quality paper. Packaging is also acid-free and fully recyclable.</p>
					</div>
					<a href="/contact" class="aside-cta">Get in touch →</a>
				</aside>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	main {
		max-width: 960px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 3em 1.5em 5em;
	}
	.page-label {
		font-size: 0.72em;
		letter-spacing: 0.18em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--cyan-mid);
		margin: 0 0 0.75em;
	}
	h1 {
		font-size: 2.4em;
		color: var(--prussian);
		line-height: 1.15;
		margin: 0 0 1.25em;
		max-width: 18ch;
	}
	h2 {
		font-size: 1.25em;
		color: var(--prussian);
		margin: 0 0 1.25em;
	}
	p {
		color: var(--text-muted);
		line-height: 1.8;
		margin: 0 0 1.1em;
		font-size: 0.95em;
	}
	.about-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 300px;
		gap: 4em;
		align-items: start;
	}
	.about-divider {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
		margin: 2em 0;
	}
	.process-list {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1.5em;
	}
	.process-item {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1.25em;
	}
	.p-num {
		font-size: 0.7em;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		color: var(--cyan-mid);
		padding-top: 0.3em;
		flex-shrink: 0;
		width: 1.5em;
	}
	.process-item strong {
		display: block;
		font-size: 0.9em;
		color: var(--prussian);
		margin-bottom: 0.3em;
	}
	.process-item p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.88em; }

	.about-aside {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1em;
		position: sticky;
		top: 2em;
	}
	.aside-card {
		background: var(--cyan-pale);
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 1.25em 1.5em;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
	}
	.aside-card h3 {
		font-size: 0.85em;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--prussian);
		margin: 0 0 0.5em;
	}
	.aside-card p { font-size: 0.82em; margin: 0; }
	.aside-cta {
		display: block;
		text-align: center;
		background: var(--prussian);
		color: var(--sand-light);
		padding: 0.85em;
		border-radius: 6px;
		text-decoration: none;
		font-size: 0.85em;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		margin-top: 0.5em;
		transition: background 0.2s;
	}
	.aside-cta:hover { background: var(--prussian-dark); color: #fff; }

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2em; }
		.about-aside { position: static; }
		h1 { font-size: 1.9em; }
	}
</style>
